    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133-a3">

                <pb facs="0281" n="225" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg225"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 76.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoffman to Lord
                            Derby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 1,
                        1876</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Referring to your note of the 11th of
                    April, and to mine of the 20th, I have the honor to request that your lordship
                    will take such steps as shall lead to the detention of the fugitive Winslow in
                    custody until I shall have received your lordship’s answer to my note, and have
                    had time to communicate it to Mr. Fish, and to receive his instructions in
                    reply.</p>
                <p>I make this request in the interest of justice, and with the earnest hope that
                    means may be found of settling the question unfortunately in dispute between our
                    two governments, and of thus preserving the treaty, and avoiding the turning of
                    great criminals loose upon society to recommence their career of crime.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WICKHAM HOFFMAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
